/* The map tab, INTERIM. The handoff's Splice World Map v2 needs eight polygon
 * regions with five yield states, Ark pins, ally and hostile markers, animated
 * collector routes and an apex vein pulse. None of the systems behind those
 * are built: /v1/region/state returns node slots and a roster headline, and
 * config/bundles/0.1.3/nodes.json is two node types with hourly rates.
 * Neither relocation nor a collector system is implemented, so there is
 * nothing to drive an overlay with.
 *
 * So this is a node LIST with the foundation applied, and it is deferred to
 * Phase 10 rather than finished here. Phase 8 design section 5.3. Do not
 * approximate the map against two node types; a polygon viewport over this
 * data would be a mock, not a screen.
 *
 * THREE CORRECTIONS TO THE PARAGRAPH ABOVE, MEASURED IN TASK 12 AGAINST THE
 * PLAN THAT WROTE IT. Each one makes the deferral narrower and better
 * evidenced, which is the point of recording them rather than quietly
 * shipping the looser claim.
 *
 * 1. "THERE IS NO GEOMETRY ANYWHERE" IS FALSE AS WRITTEN, and the true
 *    statement is narrower and more useful.
 *    specs/broodline_region_graph.md (status: current) authors THIRTY
 *    regions and forty-three edges with full adjacency, and
 *    specs/broodline_region_roster.md section 2 authors each of those
 *    thirty with a band, a lane count, a Common Vein count, Rich Deposit
 *    slots, Apex eligibility, adjacency and claimability. That is already
 *    enough to colour a region by yield.
 *
 *    What exists NOWHERE - specs, config, services or client - is
 *    COORDINATE geometry: no vertices, no polygons, no positions, nothing
 *    an outline could be drawn from. The roster says so itself, in as many
 *    words: regions differ "in look and lane arrangement only", and
 *    "visual identity is an art task". So the shapes are owed by a
 *    pipeline that does not exist rather than missing from a table.
 *
 *    None of that region data reaches the client either. The bundle has no
 *    regions.json, and /v1/region/state sends one regionId and its nodes.
 *    Worth knowing before Phase 10 starts: the handoff draws EIGHT regions
 *    where the roster authors thirty, so the two sources disagree about
 *    the map before anyone tries to draw it.
 *
 * 2. THE NODE RATE IS NOT ON THE WIRE, which is why the stat cells below
 *    state accrual and depletion rather than the plan's "rate and yield".
 *    nodes.json authors ratePerHour and totalYield and
 *    services/api/src/map/rotation.ts reads both, but RegionStateResponse's
 *    node object is slot, type, accrued, remaining, grants - and carries
 *    neither. A cell stating 20 an hour would be this client inventing a
 *    number. Richness is worse: it is a REGION property in the handoff and
 *    no region property reaches the client, so the plan's "a ProgressBar
 *    for richness" has nothing to fill and this screen draws no bar.
 *
 * 3. THERE ARE TWO NODES, NOT AN OPEN LIST. rotation.ts's nodesFor returns
 *    slot 0 Common Vein and slot 1 Rich Deposit for every region, epoch and
 *    seed - "with one region and no relocation, the epoch boundary respawns
 *    the Rich Deposit in place". So the list is two rows long in
 *    production, which is the other half of why a viewport over it would be
 *    a mock.
 *
 * SEVENTEEN DECLARATIONS LEFT THIS FILE AND SIX ARRIVED, and none of the six
 * is a copy of one that left - which is the test of whether a screen
 * composes the layer or re-derives it:
 *   - the root's `flex-direction: column` is UI Toolkit's default, and its
 *     `padding: var(--gutter)` is the scaffold's content region.
 *   - `__roster`'s row direction, wrap and bottom margin described a Label
 *     stacked above a list. It is the scaffold's header slot now, which is
 *     already a centred row, and the 12px bottom margin was the blank strip
 *     an unset roster headline drew.
 *   - `__nodes`' column is the default again.
 *   - `.node-row`'s nine - fill, radius, hairline border, padding, bottom
 *     margin, row direction, space-between, centring - are `SectionCard`
 *     plus its `.elev-1` wrapper. The class name survives as a handle and
 *     carries no rule.
 *   - `.node-row > Label`'s font-size and colour are Theme's own `Label`
 *     rule, value for value.
 *
 * THE STAT ROW IS THIS FILE'S AND NOT StatCell.uss's, for the reason that
 * sheet's closing note records: a stylesheet attached through `<ui:Style>` in
 * a component's UXML reaches that component and its descendants and never its
 * parent, so a row of cells belongs to whatever holds them.
 */
.region-view { flex-grow: 1; }

.region-view__stats { flex-direction: row; }

/* A sentence, not a label, so it wraps. The tint, radius and padding are
 * Theme's `.panel-coral` and the ink is `.t-danger`; shown only when it says
 * something - RegionView.CardFor has the measurement. */
.region-view__blocker {
    white-space: normal;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
}

/* A row action, not a screen CTA, so it sits at the card's trailing edge at
 * its own width rather than stretching. It is NOT `.btn-primary`: three
 * ramped CTAs stacked down a list would each claim to be the screen's one
 * next step. The 12px replaces Theme's 4px Button margin, which is a CTA
 * row's spacing and too tight under a wrapped refusal. */
.region-view__claim {
    align-self: flex-end;
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
}
